\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Same text, different stored value, different answer. (A)~The model wrote ``After step 5 the value is 457.'' The text never changes; the hidden state at the 457 token is overwritten with the state a run that wrote 462 would have produced, and the final answer continues from 462, a value appearing nowhere in any text. (B)~Fraction of runs whose final answer uses the injected value, per model: planting a counterfactual value (circles), restoring the correct value under corrupted text (squares), and a size-matched random control (triangles); bars are 95\% bootstrap intervals. The reasoning-distilled models re-solve after their reasoning phase, which raises their random-control rate; re-derivation can only produce the correct answer. (C,~D)~With two counters $A$ and $B$, injecting a replacement for either or both ($a'$, $b'$) makes the answer equal the matching sum; answers using only one of two injected values occur at 0.01.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:registers}{{1}{2}{Same text, different stored value, different answer. (A)~The model wrote ``After step 5 the value is 457.'' The text never changes; the hidden state at the 457 token is overwritten with the state a run that wrote 462 would have produced, and the final answer continues from 462, a value appearing nowhere in any text. (B)~Fraction of runs whose final answer uses the injected value, per model: planting a counterfactual value (circles), restoring the correct value under corrupted text (squares), and a size-matched random control (triangles); bars are 95\% bootstrap intervals. The reasoning-distilled models re-solve after their reasoning phase, which raises their random-control rate; re-derivation can only produce the correct answer. (C,~D)~With two counters $A$ and $B$, injecting a replacement for either or both ($a'$, $b'$) makes the answer equal the matching sum; answers using only one of two injected values occur at 0.01}{figure.1}{}}
